[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis 5 — special numerators**: `x == 0` (both outputs zero),
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `x == INT_MIN`, `x == INT_MAX`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis 6 — `printf("%d")` formatting shape**, the *output* axis: number of
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m digits (1, 2, 10), presence of a `-` sign in the quotient field, in the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m remainder field, in both, in neither. `%d` of `INT_MIN` is the widest possible
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m field (`-2147483648`, 11 chars) and is the only input where the digits cannot
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m be produced by negating into a positive `int`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The table below is the cross-product of axes 1–6, pruned to the combinations
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the code actually distinguishes (e.g. `|x| == |y|` forces `rem == 0`, so
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `|x|==|y|` × `inexact` is impossible and omitted; `y == 1` forces `rem == 0`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m likewise).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Every row is exercised with **many randomized inputs** drawn from that row's
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m region (fixed-seed SplitMix64 PRNG, so runs are reproducible), not one
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     55[0m:[38;5;10m[49m hand-picked value, plus the row's boundary values. Both `.so`s are called
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     56[0m:[38;5;10m[49m through their exported `driver` symbol and the captured stdout bytes are
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     57[0m:[38;5;10m[49m compared with `assert_eq!` on `Vec<u8>`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     58[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
